  "metaDescription": "Gibran Rakabuming Raka has formally stepped down as the Vice President of Indonesia, prompting President Prabowo Subianto to initiate replacement talks.",
  "aiSummaryBullets": [
    "Gibran Rakabuming Raka has officially resigned from his position as the Vice President of Indonesia.",
    "President Prabowo Subianto has accepted the resignation and expressed appreciation for the former official's two-year tenure.",
    "Presidential consultations with coalition parties are underway to propose two candidates for the vacant vice-presidential seat."
  ],
  "aiContextParagraph": "Gibran Rakabuming Raka formally concluded his tenure as Indonesia's Vice President on November 12, 2026, following a resignation process accepted by President Prabowo Subianto. Following his departure from the Vice Presidential Palace, where he was seen off by staff and supporters, the focus has shifted to the administrative procedures for his succession. Minister of Law and Human Rights Yusril Ihza Mahendra confirmed that President Prabowo is authorized to select two potential candidates to fill the vacancy, a process that involves consultations with the governing coalition parties. Additionally, the People's Consultative Assembly (MPR) is expected to declare the office vacant to facilitate the appointment of a successor. Discussions regarding the legal and procedural requirements for this transition are currently ongoing between the executive branch and legislative representatives, including the House of Representatives' Commission III.",
